### Hash Sensitive User Inputs using SHA-256

We can also use SHA-256 to hash sensitive user inputs, such as passwords and credit card numbers. This will help protect the confidentiality of the data and prevent unauthorized access.
```java
// Import necessary libraries
import java.security.MessageDigest;
import java.security.NoSuchAlgorithmException;

// Define the hash configuration
String algorithm = "SHA-256";

// Implement hashing for sensitive user inputs
public String hash(String input) {
    try {
        MessageDigest digester = MessageDigest.getInstance(algorithm);
        byte[] hash = digester.digest(input.getBytes());
        return Base64.encodeBase64String(hash);
    } catch (NoSuchAlgorithmException e) {
        System.out.println("Error hashing input: " + e.getMessage());
        throw new RuntimeException(e);
    }
}
```
