In addition to implementing data encryption for sensitive attributes, we can also use strong passwords and two-factor authentication to protect the confidentiality of the data. This will help prevent unauthorized access and ensure the security of the system.
```java
// Use strong passwords and two-factor authentication
public void login(String username, String password) {
    // Check if the user exists in the database
    if (getGraphDatabase().containsUser(username)) {
        // Validate the password using a secure hashing algorithm
        String hashedPassword = hash(password);
        if (getGraphDatabase().validateUser(username, hashedPassword)) {
            System.out.println("Login successful");
        } else {
            System.out.println("Invalid credentials");
        }
    } else {
        System.out.println("User does not exist in the database");
    }
}
