To provide user-friendly feedback to users, we can implement detailed error messages that explain the cause of the error and suggest possible solutions. This will help reduce frustration and improve the overall user experience.
```java
// Import necessary libraries
import java.util.logging.Logger;

// Define the logger configuration
Logger logger = Logger.getLogger(this.getClass().getName());

// Implement detailed error messages for user-friendly feedback
public void handleError(Exception e) {
    if (e instanceof IOException) {
        // Log the error and provide a user-friendly message
        logger.severe("An error occurred while reading from the database: " + e.getMessage());
        System.out.println("Error reading from database: " + e.getMessage());
    } else if (e instanceof IllegalArgumentException) {
        // Log the error and provide a user-friendly message
        logger.severe("An error occurred while processing input data: " + e.getMessage());
        System.out.println("Error processing input data: " + e.getMessage());
    } else if (e instanceof RuntimeException) {
        // Log the error and provide a user-friendly message
        logger.severe("An unexpected error occurred: " + e.getMessage());
        System.out.println("Unexpected error occurred: " + e.getMessage());
    } else {
        // Log the error and provide a generic message
        logger.severe("An unknown error occurred: " + e.getMessage());
        System.out.println("Unknown error occurred: " + e.getMessage());
    }
}
