To handle temporary unavailability of external systems, the code uses circuit breakers and rate limiting mechanisms to prevent cascading failures. Circuit breakers are used to detect and prevent cascading failures caused by repeated requests to an unavailable system. Rate limiting is used to prevent overloading the service with too many requests when the external systems are temporarily unavailable.

