```java
import java.util.concurrent.ConcurrentHashMap;
import java.util.concurrent.ConcurrentMap;

public class UnionFind {
    private ConcurrentMap<Node, Node> sets;

    public UnionFind() {
        this.sets = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();
    }

    public void union(Node node1, Node node2) {
        // Add two nodes to the same set if they are not already in the same set
        Node set1 = getSet(node1);
        Node set2 = getSet(node2);
        if (set1 != set2) {
            this.sets.put(set1, set2);
        }
    }

    public Node getSet(Node node) {
        // Return the representative of the set containing a given node
        return this.sets.getOrDefault(node, node);
    }
}
```
The `UnionFind` class represents a data structure for managing disjoint sets of nodes using the Union-Find algorithm. The class has two methods: `union()` which adds two nodes to the same set if they are not already in the same set, and `getSet()` which returns the representative of the set containing a given node.

```java
import java.util.Map;

public class GraphProcessor {
    private GraphDatabase graphDatabase;
    private UnionFind unionFind;
    private DataFeed dataFeed;
    private Map<Node, Integer> weightedConnections;

    public GraphProcessor(GraphDatabase graphDatabase, UnionFind unionFind, DataFeed dataFeed) {
        this.graphDatabase = graphDatabase;
        this.unionFind = unionFind;
        this.dataFeed = dataFeed;
        this.weightedConnections = new HashMap<>();
    }

    public void processGraph() {
        // Process the graph using the Union-Find algorithm and a modified version of the Weighted-Union algorithm
        for (Node node : this.graphDatabase.getNodes()) {
            Node representative = this.unionFind.getSet(node);
            if (representative == node) {
                // If the node is its own representative, it is a singleton set and we can compute its weighted connections
                this.weightedConnections.put(node, this.dataFeed.getWeight(node));
            } else {
                // If the node is not its own representative, we can add its weight to the representative's weight
                int weight = this.dataFeed.getWeight(node);
                this.weightedConnections.put(representative, this.weightedConnections.getOrDefault(representative, 0) + weight);
            }
        }
    }
}
```
The `GraphProcessor` class represents the processor of the graph and has four fields: `graphDatabase`, which is the external graph database, `unionFind`, which is the data structure for managing disjoint sets of nodes, `dataFeed`, which is a data feed from an external source, and `weightedConnections`, which is a map of weighted connections between nodes. The class also has a single method: `processGraph()` which processes the graph using the Union-Find algorithm and a modified version of the Weighted-Union algorithm."]

