The `connect_to_source` method connects to an external data source and retrieves data, and the `process_data_` method processes the data for a given tenant by transforming and normalizing it into a unified format, validating it against a schema, and writing it to the destination.

The system includes support for real-time data processing, with the ability to handle data inconsistencies, missing values, and schema mismatches gracefully. It also supports multi-tenant operations, with each tenant having unique data processing requirements and access controls. The system can dynamically adjust resource allocation based on SLA levels and overall system performance, while ensuring data integrity and producing consistent outputs.

The system is designed to be highly available, scalable, and self-adaptive, with the ability to handle large volumes of data and high traffic loads. It includes support for backup and recovery, with the ability to recover from failures and maintain consistency of data in the event of a failure.

Overall, this implementation provides a robust and scalable solution for handling large amounts of unstructured data from external sources, with the ability to handle complex processing tasks and ensure data integrity and consistency.']

