The log configuration is handled through an environment variable and a JSON-based configuration file, allowing for dynamic adjustment of log levels and destination settings without restarting the application. The logging service also implements comprehensive error handling, including retries for failed log deliveries and graceful degradation strategies when external services become unavailable.

The performance impact of using this implementation is optimized for latency under normal conditions while maintaining robustness under stress. Resource usage is also optimized through effective design patterns and modular architecture. The unit tests and integration tests cover critical paths and edge cases, ensuring reliability in production environments.']

