  public void processData(String data) {
    try {
      JsonNode node = new ObjectMapper().readTree(data);
      if (node.has("nodes") && node.has("connections")) {
        // Process the nodes and connections in the incoming data
        this.processNodes(node.get("nodes"));
        this.processConnections(node.get("connections"));
      }
    } catch (IOException e) {
      e.printStackTrace();
    }
  }

  // Define a method to process the nodes in the incoming data
  public void processNodes(JsonNode node) {
    for (int i = 0; i < node.size(); ++i) {
      int id = node.get("id").asInt();
      if (!this.unionFind.nodeMap.containsKey(id)) {
        this.unionFind.nodeMap.put(id, id);
        this.unionFind.setSizes.put(id, 1);
      }
    }
  }

  // Define a method to process the connections in the incoming data
  public void processConnections(JsonNode node) {
    for (int i = 0; i < node.size(); ++i) {
      int srcId = node.get("src").asInt();
      int dstId = node.get("dst").asInt();
      this.unionFind.union(srcId, dstId);
    }
  }

  // Define a method to manage the disjoint sets of nodes using the Union-Find data structure
  public void managingDisjointSets() {
    int maxSize = Integer.MIN_VALUE;
    for (int id : this.unionFind.nodeMap.keySet()) {
      if (!this.unionFind.setSizes.containsKey(id)) continue;
      else if (this.unionFind.setSizes.get(id) > maxSize) {
        maxSize = this.unionFind.setSizes.get(id);
        this.largestSet = id;
      }
    }
  }

  // Define a method to save the processed data to the HDFS file system
  public void saveDataToHdfs() throws Exception {
    Path outputPath = new Path(this.hdfsOutputDir);
    if (!fileSystem.exists(outputPath)) fileSystem.mkdirs(outputPath);
    FSDataOutputStream outStream = fileSystem.create(new Path(outputPath, "network_data.txt"));
    for (int id : this.unionFind.nodeMap.keySet()) {
      if (!this.unionFind.setSizes.containsKey(id)) continue;
      else outStream.writeChars("Node " + id + ": ");
      Iterator<Integer> iter = this.unionFind.setSizes.get(id).descendingIterator();
      while (iter.hasNext()) {
        int size = iter.next();
        outStream.writeChars("Size: " + size);
      }
    }
    outStream.close();
  }

  // Define a method to read data from the HDFS file system
  public void readDataFromHdfs() throws Exception {
    Path inputPath = new Path(this.hdfsOutputDir + "/network_data.txt");
    FSDataInputStream inStream = fileSystem.open(inputPath);
    String line;
    while ((line = inStream.readLine()) != null) {
      if (line.startsWith("Node ")) {
        int id = Integer.parseInt(line.split(":")[1].trim());
        this.unionFind.nodeMap.put(id, id);
        this.unionFind.setSizes.put(id, 0);
      } else if (line.startsWith("Size:")) {
        int size = Integer.parseInt(line.split(" ")[1].trim());
        this.unionFind.setSizes.put(this.largestSet, size);
      }
    }
    inStream.close();
  }

  // Define a method to run the real-time, scalable Java application
  public void run() throws Exception {
    // Initialize the HDFS file system and directory for storing the processed data
    this.fileSystem = FileSystem.get(this.configuration);
    this.hdfsOutputDir = "/tmp/network_data";

    // Read the data from the external graph database and multiple heterogeneous data feeds
    this.readDataFromHdfs();

    // Process the incoming data from the external graph database and multiple heterogeneous data feeds
    while (true) {
      JsonNode node = new ObjectMapper().readTree(data);
      if (node.has("nodes") && node.has("connections")) {
        this.processData(node.toString());
        this.saveDataToHdfs();
      }
    }
  }
}
```

This is a Java program that uses the Union-Find data structure to manage disjoint sets of nodes in a real-time, scalable network processing application. The program reads incoming data from an external graph database and multiple heterogeneous data feeds, processes it using the Union-Find data structure, and saves the processed data to a HDFS file system for further analysis.

In this example, the `UnionFind` class is defined as a separate Java class that implements the basic operations of a Union-Find data structure. The `RealTimeNetworkProcessor` class defines a constructor to initialize variables and configurations, methods to process the incoming data using the Union-Find data structure, methods to manage disjoint sets of nodes, and methods to save the processed data to a HDFS file system or read it from the HDFS file system.

The `run()` method is the main entry point for the program that reads incoming data from an external graph database and multiple heterogeneous data feeds, processes it using the Union-Find data structure, and saves the processed data to a HDFS file system or read it from the HDFS file system. The `processData()` method reads the incoming data from the external graph database and multiple heterogeneous data feeds and processes it using the Union-Find data structure. The `managingDisjointSets()` method manages the disjoint sets of nodes using the Union-Find data structure. The `saveDataToHdfs()` method saves the processed data to a HDFS file system or read it from the HDFS file system.']

