public static String reverseString(String input) {
    if (input == null || input.isEmpty()) {
        return "";
    }
    char[] chars = input.toCharArray();
    for (int i = 0; i < chars.length / 2; i++) {
        char temp = chars[i];
        chars[i] = chars[chars.length - i - 1];
        chars[chars.length - i - 1] = temp;
    }
    return new String(chars);
}
```
This function takes a string input and returns its reverse. It uses the `toCharArray()` method to convert the input string to an array of characters, and then reverses the order of the characters by swapping them with their corresponding counterparts in the last half of the array. Finally, it creates a new string from the modified character array using the constructor that takes a char array as input.

Here is an example usage of this function:
```java
String input = "hello";
System.out.println(reverseString(input)); // Output: "lohel"
