### Overriding Defaults With Command-Line Arguments

You can also use command-line arguments to override the default values in your configuration file. To do this, you can specify a list of settings and their corresponding values when starting your application. For example:

```bash
$ node app.js -m 10 -r 5
```

This will load the default values from `config.json` and override them with the values specified on the command-line.

### Overriding Defaults With Environment Variables And Command-Line Arguments

You can also use environment variables in conjunction with command-line arguments to override the default values. To do this, you can prefix the variable name with `env_` when defining the setting in your configuration file and set the corresponding environment variable before starting your application. For example:

