Here is a proposed C++ application that integrates with multiple external APIs and manages dynamic sets of dependencies to handle concurrent GET requests under varying load conditions using a connection pool to minimize latency and maximize throughput. The application also seamlessly integrates with an external configuration management system to dynamically adjust the number of active connections based on real-time server load metrics retrieved from a cloud monitoring API.
```cpp
#include <iostream>
#include <vector>
#include <string>
